      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that your worth is solely tied to a career or an achievement is a very common, but ultimately limiting, belief. Even if the academic version of you is gone, the resilience, intelligence, and drive it took to get this far are still inherently *you*. You don't need to pivot to something entirely different; you can start by exploring what parts of you felt alive *before* the pressure of that \"smart\" self took over.",
      "source": "target",
